course: dictionary
lesson: 9643
title: Sturdy and solid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sturdy means strong and solid, not easy to break or knock over. When you meet a word you don't know, ask what it describes. Here it describes things like tables, boxes and boots.
explain: «In an earthquake, people are taught to drop to the floor, take cover under a sturdy table and hold on until the shaking stops.» A table that is sturdy will not fall apart or crash down on you, so it can keep you safe. The clue is in what the table has to do: protect you.
explain: Sturdy can also describe a person or animal. «Shetland ponies from cold Scottish islands grow thick winter coats» and they are often sturdy, hardy and clever. Here sturdy means strong and healthy, with a solid body.
fact: Sturdy means strong and solid, not easy to break or knock over.
fact: «Sturdy» can describe things such as a table, a box, a desk or a pair of boots.
fact: «Sturdy» can also describe a person or animal who is strong and healthy, with a solid body.
fact: A wide base makes a structure sturdier, so a tower with a wide bottom is harder to knock over.
fact: The word changes to show more: sturdy, sturdier, sturdiest.
exercise: «Take cover under a sturdy table.» What does sturdy mean here? | Very small and light | Painted in bright colours | *Strong and solid, not easy to break | Shiny and new
exercise: Sam is going hiking and needs sturdy boots. What kind of boots does he need? | Light enough to float on water | Thin and soft like slippers | Made of paper | *Strong and solid, good for walking on rough ground
exercise: Find and copy the word in «take cover under a sturdy table» that means strong and solid. | take | cover | *sturdy | table
test: Ella says a sturdier box is one that falls apart easily. Is she right? | *Yes, it falls apart more easily | It is the same as a weaker box | No, a sturdier box is stronger and harder to break | Sturdier means painted
test: Which sentence uses sturdy to describe a person or animal? | *The sturdy pony pulled the cart all day, strong and healthy | The sturdy window broke when the ball hit it | The sturdy paper tore in the rain | The lamp was sturdy on its thin metal stick
exam: In science, a tower with a wide base is sturdier than a thin one. Why? | It is painted a bright colour | It is lighter to carry | It is taller and reaches the sky | *It is harder to knock over
